/**
 * Redeems the 4-word BIP-39 recovery code that was returned alongside
the JWT in `GET /paywall/status/{paymentHash}` after a successful
payment. The code is single-use; the server deletes it on
successful redemption.

On success the server mints a new HS256 JWT whose `expiresIn`
is clamped to the **remaining** seconds of the original paid
window (it never extends the host's paid budget) and returns
`{ token, tier, expiresAt }`.

Errors are deliberately tight to avoid information leaks:
- `400` — code is malformed (wrong word count, non-letters).
- `404` — code is unknown OR has already been redeemed. The two
  are conflated by design so a code-holder cannot probe for
  map membership.
- `410` — the underlying paid window has already expired.
- `429` — too many recovery attempts from this IP. The route is
  rate-limited per source IP to 10 attempts / 60 seconds to
  stop brute-force search of the ~44-bit code space.

Recovery codes live in memory only; a server restart wipes
them in step with the JWT signing secret.

 * @summary Redeem a one-time recovery code for a fresh JWT
 */
